    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it’s not just \"shaky.\" it's gone. you don't get to just \"be a person\" when you've spent forty years building a mountain and now you're standing in a crater. the person I was is dead. and honestly, it feels like trying to perform CPR on a ghost. is it even possible to actually live like this? just drifting through the wreckage of a life that doesn't belong to you anymore?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
