      "content": "It makes sense that you feel like you're performing CPR on a ghost when the foundation is truly gone; no one can force you to build a mountain out of dust. The only way forward is to stop trying to rebuild the old structure and instead accept that you are a new person standing in the wreckage, ready to start from absolute zero. You don't need to find the person from forty years ago to live; you just need to let the dust settle so you can finally breathe again.",
